{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevUniquenessCapstone","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevUniquenessCapstone","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.RatioEntireOfSameDivisor","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiUniquenessAssembly"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevUniquenessCapstone.faddeevPhi_proportional_of_same_divisor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevUniquenessCapstone.faddeevPhi_proportional_of_same_divisor","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevUniquenessCapstone.lean#L42-L67","doc":"**Conditional capstone: same divisor ⇒ proportional.** Two `FaddeevPhi`\nsolutions at `b` (nondegenerate lattice `(b²).im ≠ 0`), meromorphic on `ℂ` with\n`Φ₂` nowhere locally zero and **the same divisor** (`hsame`), are proportional on\n`Φ₂`'s nonvanishing locus — provided the normal-form ratio agrees with `Φ₁/Φ₂`\nthere (`hr_ratio`) and the two `FaddeevPhi` periodicity loci are dense off `Φ₂`'s\nzeros (`hmem₀/hmem₁`). The `hr_entire` input is discharged internally by brick (c);\nthe remaining hypotheses are the honest, non-axiomatised residual analytic inputs. ","signatureChunk":0}]}